1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,509
C3 is running in offline demo mode. Clue answers a business question with the known package details.

2
00:00:07,509 --> 00:00:13,142
The first message supplies the event brief. Clue asks for the missing name and email.

3
00:00:13,142 --> 00:00:19,775
The next message completes the enquiry. The local tool saves it and confirms success.

4
00:00:19,775 --> 00:00:22,689
Feedback is saved through the feedback tool.

5
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:28,813
An unknown policy is also recorded, and the assistant admits the information gap.

6
00:00:28,813 --> 00:00:36,491
The casebook contains the enquiry and both feedback records. Its JSON export is ready to download.

7
00:00:36,491 --> 00:00:44,394
C4 runs through its LangGraph workflow. Cipher searches and estimates a birthday mystery for ten guests.

8
00:00:44,394 --> 00:00:51,222
The actual observation confirms capacity, duration, and the two-hundred-forty-dollar starting price.

9
00:00:51,222 --> 00:00:59,115
Persona Studio compares the same brief across Clue, Cipher, and Muse, keeping the facts and changing the style.

10
00:00:59,115 --> 00:01:08,943
C4 also stores three records and exports JSON. These offline demos use real local tools; live model calls require a key.
